WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:02.290
Well, it's finally here.

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:08.430
It's been so long and yet the last four years,
in a sense, have flown by.

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:12.620
It's Election Day and I could say many different
things today.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:19.410
And if I said anything targeted at affecting
how or whether you vote, it would likely be

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:25.060
too late because most people have already
voted with early voting and absentee ballots.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:31.570
And by the time today's show goes out, my
guess is something like 95 percent will have

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:32.810
already voted.

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:38.069
Just remaining with the last few to vote in
person in the second half of today.

00:00:38.069 --> 00:00:42.210
And the reality is that at this point, this
election has been decided.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:45.820
We won't know the results until the ballots
are counted.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:48.979
Hopefully every single ballot will be counted.

00:00:48.979 --> 00:00:52.780
That's an entire other issue that we've been
dealing with this election.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:59.030
But this is one of the largest inflection
points, not just in American, but in global

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:01.920
politics that I've lived through.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:06.610
And certainly the biggest inflection point
that I've covered since starting The David

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:08.990
Pakman Show years and years ago.

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:12.720
It is not just the presidency that is up for
grabs tonight.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.740
Yes, in a literal sense, it is also the Senate.

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:20.399
We don't know whether Republicans will retain
control or not.

00:01:20.399 --> 00:01:24.899
It is also the House of Representatives, although
Democrats are not just expected to retain

00:01:24.899 --> 00:01:29.509
control there, but even to expand the Democratic
majority in the House of Representatives.

00:01:29.509 --> 00:01:34.829
But it is really I don't want to be hyperbolic,
but there's and I'm not.

00:01:34.829 --> 00:01:37.750
But it sounds like hyperbolic language.

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:45.380
The next 10 to 20 years of American politics
and global politics, I believe, are tied up

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:51.950
in the results today that we will start to
get tonight the future of the United States

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:58.939
as either part of the solution or part of
the problem on climate depends on whether

00:01:58.939 --> 00:02:03.289
Donald Trump gets reelected today and whether
Democrats take the Senate today.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:08.250
The future of the American reputation and
by extension, the experience that all of us

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:14.150
have in the world, both when we are in the
United States and when we travel elsewhere.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:16.840
That is at stake today.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:23.870
And also at stake today is whether we start
to disassemble this mind virus that is Trump

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:33.180
ism or whether it is reinforced and perpetuated
over the next four years, which would be an

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:35.370
unconscionable disaster.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:41.430
Donald Trump is uniquely unqualified to be
president of the United States at any time.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:47.170
But there could be no worse time for such
an unqualified and incompetent president than

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:48.470
right now.

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:52.440
We've been faced with a 100 year global pandemic.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:57.630
Any other American president from the last
hundred years would have better handled this

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:58.630
pandemic.

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:05.910
And in fact, I would suggest that just about
any thinking person would have better handled

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:11.790
this pandemic by stepping aside and saying,
I know enough to know when I don't know and

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.440
I'm going to let the experts handle this.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:18.770
It's almost as if saying nothing and just
saying I'm going to let other people handle

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:21.400
handle it would have been better and in fact,
it would have been better.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:27.070
And Donald Trump deserves to be powerfully
repudiated and removed because of his mishandling

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:28.470
of the pandemic.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:33.620
We are rapidly approaching a record hurricane
season caused by many things.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:39.670
One component of which is believed to be warmer
oceans, partially as a result of American

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:42.150
and human activity on planet Earth.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.610
It is the United States is a polluter.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:45.470
It is humans as polluters.

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:47.460
That is a factor in this.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.680
Worse, potentially worse than ever.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:50.680
Hurricane season.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:56.370
And we have a president who has said climate
change is a Chinese hoax meant to bolster

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.970
the Chinese manufacturing industry.

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:04.640
We have an economic crisis which will likely
get worse before it gets better with the third

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.700
spike of Corona virus coming in the United
States.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:12.480
And we have a president who knows nothing
about economics, who called his later to be

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:17.500
indicted national security adviser in the
middle of the night to say, hey, is a strong

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:20.780
dollar good or bad for the United States?

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:24.140
That's who is handling the economic situation.

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:30.260
We've had Great Depression like unemployment
numbers, GDP declines that even with the partial

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:35.100
recovery of the third quarter, leave us eight
percent shy of where we were at the start

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.260
of the pandemic.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:40.850
Eight percent when you talk about GDP is a
monstrous number.

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:46.490
And we have a global community that started
by laughing at us, but they're not laughing

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:47.490
anymore.

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:50.190
They are actually scared and pitying us.

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:55.150
Listen to the foreign callers who called into
my streams over the last week from Austria

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:58.410
and Argentina and Australia and Spain, the
United.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:00.310
Kingdom, France, where else?

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:06.800
Many, many places they are scared of Trump
and they fear for our futures.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:10.800
There would be no time in American history
where Donald Trump would have been a good

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:11.800
president.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:17.390
But there are times in American history where
he could have been a more benign annoyance.

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:22.880
There is no time in American history worse
than right now for a president that has so

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:29.680
weaponized the worst of the electorate and
has so coalesced the most disgusting and violent

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:32.190
instances of the American right wing.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:38.780
We tried the businessman President Mitt Romney,
tried to do it, and the country was very soundly

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:41.730
said, no, we are reelecting Barack Obama.

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:45.530
We now tried the businessman president and
it failed.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:51.360
Bad relationships need a clean end and we
can elect a different spouse today for lack

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:55.150
of a better term and get a clean break on
January 20th.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:06:00.370
You don't usually get the divorce and the
new marriage on the same day, but we actually

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:01.800
have that opportunity.

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:04.490
I don't know who's ultimately going to win
tonight.

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:08.770
I don't know when we will ultimately know
the results and win or lose tonight unless

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:13.880
we fix our education, our culture of our financial
systems.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:19.440
We aren't going to fix the problem of 30,
40, 50, 60 million people who not only voted

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:23.490
for Donald Trump four years ago, but after
seeing what he did for the last four years,

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:25.139
said, give me another four.

00:06:25.139 --> 00:06:31.139
OK. Trump ism does not disappear with Trump,
whether he leaves in two and a half months

00:06:31.139 --> 00:06:34.040
or four years and two and a half months.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:39.490
If there are no consequences for the disgusting,
bad faith politics that we've seen this cycle,

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:44.260
and in fact, if we don't deal with that, it
could continue indefinitely.

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:46.889
It could even be the downfall of the country.

00:06:46.889 --> 00:06:51.340
And I know many will say the United States
could never have a downfall.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:53.240
It's too powerful.

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:59.720
Every empire in the midst would say we will
last forever.

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:03.750
And just about every such empire did eventually
fall.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:05.480
But we're getting ahead of ourselves.

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:06.800
Did you vote?

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:07.800
Is the.

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:08.800
If the answer.

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:09.800
Yes.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:12.810
If the answer is yes, then you've done your
part.

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:15.530
Did you tell people you should vote?

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:20.220
And here's why you should vote for Joe Biden
or some combination, some version of that.

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:21.630
We have to be OK.

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:25.800
Knowing we've done what we can do, we ultimately
don't control the fact that there are more

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:30.680
than 60 million people in this country likely
to vote vote to reelect Donald Trump.

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:34.100
But for today, the focus is let's remove Trump.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:36.250
Let's take control of the Senate back.

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:39.640
Let's open the door to starting to fix some
of these issues.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:40.710
The counterpoint.

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:43.110
The alternative is very ugly.

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:48.640
And it's not clear to me that our democracy
can withstand another four years of Trump.

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:54.480
The country will withstand four more years
of Trump, but will our democracy?

00:07:54.480 --> 00:08:01.889
And by the way, another four years of Trump
opens the door to another Trump in 2024.

00:08:01.889 --> 00:08:07.400
It could be literally another Trump like Donald
Trump Junior or Ivanka Trump.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:09.750
It could just be a Trump like Republican.

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:11.290
Both would be a disaster.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:15.180
So today is not about reminding you about
bleach injections.

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:20.460
Drawing on hurricane maps with sharpies like
the one I have here, or lying again and again

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:23.669
and again and again and again, as he has done
for so long.

00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:29.570
This is merely about saying to the world through
the results that we will hopefully get today.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:33.899
Enough of us realize the mistake that was
made in 2016.

00:08:33.899 --> 00:08:38.659
Some of us made a mistake by actually voting
for Trump, not me, but some of us did.

00:08:38.659 --> 00:08:42.039
Some of us made a mistake by not voting at
all.

00:08:42.039 --> 00:08:47.119
We realized that mistake and we are test taking
not even step one, but step zero point five

00:08:47.119 --> 00:08:48.800
in the direction of fix fixing it.

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:52.480
We're trying to get the ball back to try to
put some points on the board in the next couple

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:53.480
of years.

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:56.019
I hope everyone in the audience has voted.

00:08:56.019 --> 00:09:00.649
We will be hopefully all together tonight
as the results start to come in.

00:09:00.649 --> 00:09:06.019
We may not know everything by by midnight
tonight, but we will know quite a bit.

00:09:06.019 --> 00:09:09.709
And we will do our best to get you ready today
for the next 24 hours.

